{"id":"789230403cc61bdd","group":"58","path":"58/batch09/58-thm-bsdm.md","title":"conj-bsd — Birch–Swinnerton-Dyer Conjecture","display":"conj-bsd — Birch–Swinnerton-Dyer Conjecture","type":"conjecture","metadata":{"type":"conjecture","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-conj-bsd","aliases":["58-conj-bsd","58-thm-bsdm"],"display":"conj-bsd — Birch–Swinnerton-Dyer Conjecture","depends_on":["[[58-df-l-series]]","[[58-df-elliptic-curve]]","[[58-df-rank]]","[[58-df-field]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"conjecture"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-conj-bsd"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-conj-bsd</span><span>58-thm-bsdm</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"conj-bsd — Birch–Swinnerton-Dyer Conjecture"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"adeb1236931d5593\" href=\"?note=adeb1236931d5593\" title=\"58-df-l-series\">58-df-l-series</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"74f4744df7db749f\" href=\"?note=74f4744df7db749f\" title=\"58-df-elliptic-curve\">58-df-elliptic-curve</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"39b5d097687ec105\" href=\"?note=39b5d097687ec105\" title=\"58-df-rank\">58-df-rank</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"1eb4a89b005d9cda\" href=\"?note=1eb4a89b005d9cda\" title=\"58-df-field\">58-df-field</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E\\in\\operatorname{Ell}(\\mathbb Q)\">\\(E\\in\\operatorname{Ell}(\\mathbb Q)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L_E:\\mathbb C\\to\\mathbb C\">\\(L_E:\\mathbb C\\to\\mathbb C\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r=\\operatorname{rank}E(\\mathbb Q)\">\\(r=\\operatorname{rank}E(\\mathbb Q)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\unicode{x0428}(E),\\Omega_E,\\operatorname{Reg}_E,\\langle c_p:p\\in\\mathbb P\\rangle,E(\\mathbb Q)_{\\mathrm{tors}}\\in V\">\\(\\unicode{x0428}(E),\\Omega_E,\\operatorname{Reg}_E,\\langle c_p:p\\in\\mathbb P\\rangle,E(\\mathbb Q)_{\\mathrm{tors}}\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BSD}_S\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{BSD}_S\\subseteq V\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{conj\\text{-}bsd} \\vdash \\mathrm{BSD}_S(E)\\leftrightarrow |\\unicode{x0428}(E)|&lt;\\aleph_0\\land\\operatorname{ord}_{s=1}L_E(s)=r\\land\\lim_{s\\to1}\\frac{L_E(s)}{(s-1)^r}=\\frac{|\\unicode{x0428}(E)|\\,\\Omega_E\\,\\operatorname{Reg}_E\\prod_{p\\in\\mathbb{Prime}} c_p}{\\lvert E(\\mathbb Q)_{\\mathrm{tors}}\\rvert^2}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{conj\\text{-}bsd} \\vdash \\mathrm{BSD}_S(E)\\leftrightarrow |\\unicode{x0428}(E)|&lt;\\aleph_0\\land\\operatorname{ord}_{s=1}L_E(s)=r\\land\\lim_{s\\to1}\\frac{L_E(s)}{(s-1)^r}=\\frac{|\\unicode{x0428}(E)|\\,\\Omega_E\\,\\operatorname{Reg}_E\\prod_{p\\in\\mathbb{Prime}} c_p}{\\lvert E(\\mathbb Q)_{\\mathrm{tors}}\\rvert^2}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The modularity theorem supplies analytic continuation and a functional equation for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L_E(s)\">\\(L_E(s)\\)</span> when <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E/\\mathbb Q\">\\(E/\\mathbb Q\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The finiteness of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\unicode{x0428}(E)\">\\(\\unicode{x0428}(E)\\)</span> is now an explicit conjunct rather than an unstated precondition for writing its cardinality in the leading-coefficient formula.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":